Subject: fix(cli): address the configured forge in the three remaining GitHub clients

Three code paths still named api.github.com after the agents-repo fallback and
the run's own status comment were moved onto the configured host. On an
enterprise install or an emulator, where every workflow sets GITHUB_API_URL,
each one leaves the appliance and is refused, and each logs on every run:

  ! Token scope check: fetching token scope: listing installation repositories:
    Get "https://api.github.com/installation/repositories?per_page=100": dial tcp
    140.82.112.5:443: connect: connection refused
  ! Could not resolve fullsend-ai/agents@main: get ref fullsend-ai/agents@heads/main:
    http GET /repos/fullsend-ai/agents/git/ref/heads/main: Get "https://api.github.com/...":
    dial tcp ...: connect: connection refused
  Error: listing comments: list issue comments page 1: http GET
    /repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n>/comments?per_page=100&page=1: Get
    "https://api.github.com/...": dial tcp ...: connect: connection refused
  ::warning::Could not reconcile orphaned status comment

The first two are warnings. The third is not harmless: `reconcile-status` is
the post-job step that finalizes a status comment left in the "Started" state
when the fullsend process died without posting its completion. It built its
client with a bare gh.New, which targets api.github.com regardless of
GITHUB_API_URL, so on any other host the safety net never reaches the forge
and a hard-killed or cancelled run keeps its "Started" comment forever. The
completion comment the run posts about itself already goes through
newGitHubLiveClient; this makes its fallback do the same.

The token-scope check (run.go) passed the literal "https://api.github.com" as
the base URL. It now asks tokenScopeBaseURL, which returns GITHUB_API_URL when
set and the public host otherwise, so the introspection reaches the forge that
minted the token. The eval-measure fetch context (evalmeasure.go) resolves the
measurement manifest in fullsend-ai/agents through a bare gh.New too, and now
uses newGitHubLiveClient like the harness fallback next to it.

All three keep the public host as the default, so behaviour on github.com is
unchanged. One test per site: tokenScopeBaseURL with and without the
variable, and the base URL of the client each of the other two constructs.

Breadboard note: patches Go source, so it belongs to the build patch list in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh rather than the mirror list; the mirror
patches files a workflow reads at run time, and these do not survive
compilation. Written to be sent upstream as-is, as one more facet of the host
assumption that 0005, 0007, 0008 and 0011 fix. Add a DCO sign-off before
submitting it as a human-authored change.

